WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:05.100
Mike Myers made the jump from Saturday Night
Live to the big screen with Wayne's World,

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:09.980
became a superstar with Austin Powers, and
a household name thanks to Shrek.

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:12.980
And then he seemed to pretty much drop off
the face of the Earth.

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:13.980
But why?

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:18.480
Mike Myers' movies and characters have left
a mark on popular culture that few other comedy

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:23.410
stars could ever hope to match, and his ability
to wring laughs from so many different concepts

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:24.410
is legendary.

00:00:24.410 --> 00:00:28.420
So where'd he go — and when can we expect
him to make his eventual comeback?

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:32.610
Here's the real reason why Hollywood stopped
casting Mike Myers.

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:33.610
Hobbies

00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:37.829
During his time out of the spotlight, Myers
has kept busy with a number of hobbies, ranging

00:00:37.829 --> 00:00:41.780
from playing in a floor hockey league twice
a week to Dungeons and Dragons.

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:46.179
He's a well-known major hockey fan, often
attending Toronto Maple Leafs games and sharing

00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:49.070
his thoughts on the occasional NHL broadcast.

00:00:49.070 --> 00:00:52.520
When you're rich and having fun, why bother
working if you don't have to?

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:55.969
"But what I'd really love, is to do Wayne's
World for a living.

00:00:55.969 --> 00:00:57.370
It might happen.

00:00:57.370 --> 00:00:58.370
Ya!

00:00:58.370 --> 00:01:01.109
And monkeys might fly outa my butt!"

00:01:01.109 --> 00:01:02.109
Directing

00:01:02.109 --> 00:01:05.030
Another big reason Myers hasn't been in front
of the camera in recent years?

00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:08.040
Well, he's been spending time behind it instead.

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:13.610
In 2014, Myers directed Supermensch, a documentary
about the life of Shep Gordon, a legendary

00:01:13.610 --> 00:01:18.250
music manager whose clients ranged from Blondie
and Luther Vandross to Alice Cooper.

00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:22.890
Cooper introduced Gordon to Myers after making
a cameo in Wayne's World, and Gordon has since

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:27.500
served as a mentor to the actor, even taking
the star into his home for two months after

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:29.300
the death of Myers's father.

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:30.300
Pigeonholed

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:34.280
Mike Myers is understandably known as a comedian
first and foremost.

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:39.030
But while other comedians such as Robin Williams
were able to transition into serious roles,

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:44.500
Myers remains typecast despite dramatic turns
in films like Studio 54 and Quentin Tarantino's

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:45.890
Inglorious Basterds.

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:50.500
It could be that Hollywood believes audiences
only want to see Myers cracking jokes, preventing

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:53.500
him from exploring his full acting range.

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:54.830
Flops and bombs

00:01:54.830 --> 00:01:59.880
For younger audiences who may not necessarily
associate Myers with Austin Powers or Shrek,

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:03.610
there's another movie that unfortunately comes
to mind: The Love Guru.

00:02:03.610 --> 00:02:08.979
The 2008 comedy presented Myers as, well,
a love guru whose dream is to be featured

00:02:08.979 --> 00:02:10.560
on The Oprah Winfrey Show.

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:15.230
He brought his Austin Powers costar Verne
Troyer to the film along with several big

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:18.740
names, including Justin Timberlake, Jessica
Alba, and Ben Kingsley.

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:23.550
But the film was a massive box office bomb
and a critical disaster as well.

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:25.230
Myers hasn't made a movie since.

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:31.340
"What the hell happened to you?!"

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:32.340
Bestselling author

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:37.200
During his time away from filmmaking, Myers
filled his time becoming a bestselling author,

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:39.120
penning a book called Canada.

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:43.670
The book explores what his beloved country
means to him via photographs, anecdotes, and

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:45.040
his trademark humor.

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:49.459
It was a massive success north of the border,
with Myers embarking on a nationwide promotional

00:02:49.459 --> 00:02:52.710
tour to celebrate both his book and his homeland.

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:53.710
Choosy

00:02:53.710 --> 00:02:57.780
Even if Hollywood wanted to cast Myers, they'd
have to come up with a pretty amazing script

00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:00.120
to drag him away from all of his other passions.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:03.850
So far, according to Myers, they haven't even
bothered trying.

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:09.440
He told GQ in 2014 that he had only received
15 scripts in the last quarter century, in

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:12.709
part because "I do turn virtually everything
down."

00:03:12.709 --> 00:03:16.870
Given his reputation as such a tough sell,
it's no surprise he hasn't been getting as

00:03:16.870 --> 00:03:18.750
many offers as he used to.

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:19.750
"Zip it."

00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:20.750
"You can't even-"

00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:21.750
"Zip it!"

00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:22.750
"Zip..."

00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:23.750
"Look all-"

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:26.180
"Ladies and gentlemen of the jury Exzipit
A."

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:27.739
Television disappointment

00:03:27.739 --> 00:03:34.680
In early 2015, HBO announced Myers had signed
a two-year deal with the network to make…something.

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:39.120
Details were never specified, and the following
year, it was reported that Myers eventually

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:44.100
opted out of the contract because his production
deal never led to an order of his series.

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:47.989
It's unfortunate that this particular deal
never panned out, but it signals that Myers

00:03:47.989 --> 00:03:52.400
is interested in returning to television,
either as a director, producer, or even an

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:53.930
actor.

00:03:53.930 --> 00:03:54.930
Fatherhood

00:03:54.930 --> 00:03:59.220
Myers has also been busy playing a couple
of other major roles: husband and father.

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:03.650
He and his second wife, Kelly Tisdale, recently
welcomed a new addition to their family, a

00:04:03.650 --> 00:04:05.590
daughter named Paulina Kathleen.

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:10.180
She's merely the latest in a line of kids
that includes son Spike and daughter Sunday

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:11.180
Molly.

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:12.819
How important is family life to Myers?

00:04:12.819 --> 00:04:17.780
In an interview with Deadline he said, "Anyone
who tells you fatherhood is the greatest thing

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:20.209
that can happen to you, they are understating
it.

00:04:20.209 --> 00:04:22.630
I am the happiest I have ever been in my life.

00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:26.750
I knew I wanted to be a father, I didn’t
know it was going to be this awesome or that

00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:30.260
my kid would come out so beautiful and lovely."

00:04:30.260 --> 00:04:34.160
It's tough to imagine Myers is eager to star
in anything that would take him away from

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:35.160
his family.

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:36.180
What's next?

00:04:36.180 --> 00:04:40.660
Mike Myers' incredible success with a string
of early hits might have established unreasonable

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:42.880
expectations for his later efforts.

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:46.870
But it also gave him the financial freedom
to pick his projects carefully — and that's

00:04:46.870 --> 00:04:51.400
exactly what he's done over the last several
years, taking the time to indulge outside

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:53.960
interests while waiting on the perfect script.

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:58.600
Happily for fans, that dry spell may soon
come to an end: Myers is attached to return

00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:04.500
for a fifth Shrek movie, due to arrive in
2019, and he's also booked another non-comedy,

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:09.340
signing on to star in the "noir thriller"
Terminal alongside Margot Robbie and Simon

00:05:09.340 --> 00:05:10.340
Pegg.

00:05:10.340 --> 00:05:12.810
He's even open to the idea of a third Wayne's
World movie.

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:15.000
There's only one thing to say to that.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:16.090
"Party on Wayne."

00:05:16.090 --> 00:05:17.540
"Party on Garth, alright!

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:18.880
Excellent, excellent, ok."

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:20.120
Thanks for watching!

00:05:20.120 --> 00:05:23.090
